**Replace `YOUR-ORG` with your actual GitHub organization name.**

### One change I'd recommend

I **wouldn't make Cybersecurity the default owner of the entire repository**. That's why the example uses DevOps as the default and assigns specialized areas to the appropriate teams.

Also, CODEOWNERS only makes sense when the corresponding directories exist. For example, if your analytics code isn't actually under `/data/` or `/analytics/`, change those paths to your real structure.

A good eventual structure would be:

```text
project/
├── frontend/          → Frontend
├── backend/           → Backend
├── analytics/         → Data Analytics
├── security/          → Cybersecurity
├── infrastructure/    → DevOps
├── .github/           → DevOps
├── README.md
├── CONTRIBUTING.md
└── .gitignore
````
